KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pair<DS,DS> constructed with a member unordered_map present: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/2: a class template specialization named where a
completely-defined type is required must be implicitly instantiated.  A member
std::unordered_map<DS,DS> leaves std::pair<DS,DS> registered but incomplete
(referenced under skip_typechecking_elaborate while type-checking a libstdc++
typedef), and it is never later elaborated, so the explicit construction
std::pair<DS,DS>(a,b) reports "found no match for symbol 'pair'".  This is the
root of the goto-cc cascade on rename_symbol.cpp / replace_symbol.cpp.  Flip to
CORE once fixed.
